# Accessibility baseline (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Accessibility is source code, not a plugin. Do not add accessiBe, UserWay, or similar overlays.

- Semantic landmarks: header, nav, main, footer. Skip link to `#main`.
- Keyboard: every menu, dialog, form, and CTA. Escape closes dialogs. Focus returns to the opener.
- Visible `:focus-visible`. Do not set `outline: none` without a replacement.
- Contrast AA for body text (4.5:1). Dark ember/soot palettes must be checked, not assumed.
- Errors are text in the DOM (`role="alert"`), not color-only borders.
- Labels on every input. Required state announced.
- Meaningful images get descriptive alt. Decorative images get `alt=""`.
- ARIA only when native HTML cannot express the control.
- `prefers-reduced-motion` disables entrance animation.
- Primary targets at least 44px. Zoom is never disabled.
- FAQ and product facts remain on pages without the chatbot.
- Run `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` and axe/Playwright before calling a site done.
- Ship `/accessibility` with a contact method. Log issues. Do not claim certification.

US Title II for governments currently cites WCAG 2.1 AA. Conforming to 2.2 AA covers 2.1 AA. Use 2.2 AA on every Elevate / AlbertaWeb.Design build.
